                        ],
                        "form": "sortileges"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "acfcec40-c859-3ebe-891e-2d86c51ab18c",
                        "entry_id": "d7f5db70-92fc-3062-821a-927f58a9193a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Witchcraft, magic, especially as a means of making decisions or predictions."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0e0caa36-3d74-42e1-aad0-0914f14b64b8",
                                "sense_id": "acfcec40-c859-3ebe-891e-2d86c51ab18c",
                                "text": "We have therefore summoned to our presence a Jewish woman, by name Rebecca, daughter of Isaac of York — a woman infamous for sortileges and for witcheries."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "43e363f0-2a0c-41bd-a814-cbdd61dcc309",
                                "sense_id": "acfcec40-c859-3ebe-891e-2d86c51ab18c",
                                "text": "Orthodox believers […] were less happy about using sortilege to coerce God into taking decisions on their behalf."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9e226dc9-2243-40d2-b76e-037966b15a90",
                                "sense_id": "acfcec40-c859-3ebe-891e-2d86c51ab18c",
                                "text": "‘Too much evil sortilege,’ Glad always says when someone suggests he open a franchise over Cheat Ridge."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a959e11-63fc-4f1b-b41d-f5963f9b63e3",
                                "sense_id": "acfcec40-c859-3ebe-891e-2d86c51ab18c",
                                "text": "People who faced difficult decisions or needed insight into the future would consult a diviner, who performed a ritual to locate an oracle in the codex and then interpreted the divinatory text. In Egypt and the wider Mediterranean world, this practice - sortilege - was both common and controversial."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
